<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Ag details crop growth to June 22.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Ag details crop growth to June 22.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Agriculture on Tuesday detailed the development of its major cereal, oilseed</p>
<p>and pulse crops as of Sunday, June 22.</p>
<p>CEREALS    PRE-EMERG EMERGED TILLERED JOINTED SHOTBLADE HEADED</p>
<p>June 22     1 pct     9 pct  58 pct   28 pct   4 pct     0 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg   2 pct    20 pct  61 pct   15 pct   2 pct     0 pct</p>
<p>CANOLA     PRE-EMERG EMERGED SEEDLING ROSETTE FLOWERING</p>
<p>June 22     1 pct    10 pct  51 pct   35 pct   3 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg   4 pct    25 pct  53 pct   17 pct   1 pct</p>
<p>FLAX	 PRE-EMERG EMERGED SEEDLING TILLER  FLOWERING</p>
<p>June 22     2 pct    14 pct  64 pct   20 pct   0 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg   3 pct    26 pct  59 pct   12 pct   0 pct</p>
<p>PULSE CROP PRE-EMERG EMERGED VEGETAT. FLOWERING</p>
<p>June 22     0 pct    15 pct  83 pct    2 pct</p>
<p>June 24/96  1 pct    32 pct  67 pct    0 pct</p>
<p>FALL CROPS TILLERED JOINTED SHOTBLADE HEADED   DOUGH</p>
<p>June 22     2 pct     2 pct  17 pct   64 pct   15 pct</p>
<p>92/96 Avg   2 pct     5 pct  16 pct   65 pct   12 pct</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
